# Stock Screener - Cursor Rules

This file is a legacy fallback for Cursor versions that don't read
`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. The actual rules live in two places — **do not add
new rule content here**, it will drift:

1. [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — canonical, tool-agnostic repo rules (mandatory
   formatting/testing/docs/data-layer requirements, permanent development rules,
   and multi-platform parity).
2. [`.cursor/rules/`](.cursor/rules/) — Cursor-native glob-scoped rules:
   `general.mdc`, `backend.mdc`, `frontend.mdc`, `testing.mdc`,
   `documentation.mdc`, `jira.mdc`. These are picked up automatically per
   file glob and contain code templates and workspace-specific guidance.

Read `AGENTS.md` first, then whichever `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` matches the
files you're editing. Verify rule synchronization anytime rules change with
`yarn rules:check`.
